on $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,3)$, $(-2,0)$ and $(2,-1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(8,-16)$\n- **II.** $(-6,12)$\n- **III.** $(8,16)$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186275179 :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 6 & 12 & -16\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-3,6)$, $(-6,12)$ and $(8,-16).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 6 & 12 & -16\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-3,6)$, $(-6,12)$ and $(8,-16).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""] [:db/cas 17592186275180 :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,-1)$, $(1,0)$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following ar